                <pb facs="0245" n="151" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg151"/>

                <head>No. 117.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Roberts to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 11, 1886</date>.
                        (Received December 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Chili is about to convert her foreign debt,
                    amounting to $30,000,000 into 4½ per cent. interest-bearing bonds, which she has
                    negotiated with Rothschilds of London at 96 net.</p>
                <p>By this conversion Chili will save annually in interest $1,455,733.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William R.
                    Roberts.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
